[E0352] Error: an `if` without `else` adds nothing to a list
    ╭─[ err/196_built_lists/main.wip:30:22 ]
    │
 30 │     val xs = own [1, if c { 2 }]
    │                      ─────┬────  
    │                           ╰────── no value, and no `yield`
    │ 
    │ Help: hand the value to a list built as it runs, `own [if c { yield x }]`, or give the `if` an `else`
    │ 
    │ Note: an `if` without `else` is a statement; among a list's elements, what it yields is what it adds
────╯
[E0353] Error: a list whose elements are yielded is built with `own`
    ╭─[ err/196_built_lists/main.wip:34:18 ]
    │
 34 │     val xs = [1, if c { yield 2 }]
    │                  ────────┬───────  
    │                          ╰───────── its `yield`s decide how long it is
    │ 
    │ Help: build it on the heap, with `own`
    │ 
    │ Note: a list whose `yield`s decide its length is an `own<[T]>`, built as it runs, and `own` says where it goes; a loop standing alone for a value is a generator, which yields one value at a time as it is asked
────╯
